---
/**
 * Landing hero.
 *
 * The old version listed three job titles (Product Designer · UX Strategist ·
 * Front-End) which read as three competing identities rather than one claim.
 * The h1 now makes a single claim and the line under it names the practices as
 * services under that claim.
 */
---

<section class="page-section flex min-h-[78vh] flex-col items-center justify-center text-center">
  <p
    data-hero
    class="mb-8 text-[0.7rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.36em] text-accent-text"
  >
    India · Working globally · Open for 2026
  </p>

  <h1
    data-hero
    class="hero-title text-balance text-4xl font-light leading-[1.02] text-foreground sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl"
  >
    I design complex software — <span class="text-accent-text">then I build it.</span>
  </h1>

  <p data-hero class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-base text-muted sm:text-lg">
    Product design, UX architecture, and production front-end for data &amp; AI platforms.
  </p>

  <p data-hero class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-7 text-subtle sm:text-base sm:leading-8">
    Ten years making intimidating enterprise software — iPaaS, agentic AI, WealthTech — into
    products people will actually open. I do the strategy, the system, and the code that ships,
    which means fewer handoffs and no gap between the design and what gets built.
  </p>

  <div data-hero class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
    <a href="#work" class="button-primary px-6 py-3 text-sm">See my work</a>
    <a href="/resume" data-transition class="button-secondary px-6 py-3 text-sm">
      Read the resume
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
